  <h2>About Dr. Benny</h2>
  <p>
    Dr. Ann Benny Stephen earned her doctorate from <strong>Drexel University</strong> and completed her clinical internship at <strong>Loyola University Medical Center</strong>. Her practice emphasizes the often-overlooked relationship between hearing loss and cognitive function — and the importance of evaluating both the ear and the brain together.
  </p>
  <p>
    At Duet Hearing, Dr. Benny works one-on-one with patients to design care plans that combine diagnostic precision with the brain-first principles of the DUET Method<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup>. She is a strong advocate for comprehensive auditory and brain health assessment as a foundation of preventive care.
  </p>

  <h2>Credentials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Doctor of Audiology — Drexel University</li>
    <li>Clinical Internship — Loyola University Medical Center</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Philosophy</h2>
  <blockquote>
    "Hearing loss is rarely just about the ears. The earlier we measure how your brain is processing sound, the more we can protect your cognitive future."
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Areas of Focus</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Comprehensive diagnostic audiology</li>
    <li>Hearing and cognitive health assessment</li>
    <li>Ear to Brain Evaluation<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup></li>
    <li>Patient education and prevention planning</li>
  </ul>
</PersonProfile>
